{"name":"Key West Zenith","hex":"#759fc1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"key","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Kupia."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An object designed to open and close a lock or to activate or deactivate something, especially a length of metal inserted into a narrow opening on the lock to which it is matched (keyed).","A card or fob that electronically signals a lock to open."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key"},{"term":"west","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The direction opposite to that of the earth's rotation, specifically 270°.","The western region or area; the inhabitants thereof. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Situated or lying in or toward the west; westward.","Of wind: from the west."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/west"},{"term":"zenith","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The point in the sky vertically above a given position or observer; the point in the celestial sphere opposite the nadir.","The highest point in the sky reached by a celestial body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zenith"}],"entries":[{"title":"Key West","blocks":[{"text":"Key West is a coral cay island in the Straits of Florida, at the southernmost end of the U.S. state of Florida and its outlying Florida Keys archipelago. Together with all or parts of the separate islands of Dredgers Key, Fleming Key, Sunset Key, and the northern part of Stock Island, it constitutes the City of Key West."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Southernmost_point_buoy%2C_NE_view.jpg/330px-Southernmost_point_buoy%2C_NE_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_West","wikidata":"Q485186"},{"title":"West","blocks":[{"text":"West is one of the four cardinal directions or points of the compass. It is the opposite direction from east and is the direction in which the Sun sets on the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Compass_Rose_English_West.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_West.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West","wikidata":"Q679"},{"title":"Zenith","blocks":[{"text":"The zenith is the imaginary point on the celestial sphere directly \"above\" a particular location. \"Above\" means in the vertical direction opposite to the gravity direction at that location (nadir). The zenith is the \"highest\" point on the celestial sphere. The direction opposite of the zenith is the nadir."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Zenith-Nadir-Horizon.svg/330px-Zenith-Nadir-Horizon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zenith","wikidata":"Q82806"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Key_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg/500px-Key_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Key_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg/1280px-Key_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Key_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg/500px-Key_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKey_West%2C_Florida_by_Planet_Labs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Key_West_Lighthouse_20080728.jpg/500px-Key_West_Lighthouse_20080728.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.or